{"id": "EUVD-2026-55293", "enisaUuid": "b7872ca0-0fe3-3c15-875a-910910b15ee8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: brcmfmac: make release_scratchbuffers idempotent\n\nbrcmf_pcie_release_scratchbuffers() frees the shared.scratch and\nshared.ringupd DMA buffers with dma_free_coherent() but does not clear\nthe pointers afterwards, unlike the sibling release_ringbuffers() which\nNULLs commonrings/flowrings/idxbuf on release.\n\nBoth the bus_reset .reset callback (brcmf_pcie_reset) and\nbrcmf_pcie_remove() call release_scratchbuffers.  When reset teardown\nhas run before removal, remove's own teardown would call\ndma_free_coherent() a second time on the already-freed DMA allocation.\n\nNULL the pointers after free, matching release_ringbuffers(), so a later\nrelease observes that the allocation has already been released.  This\npatch makes repeated sequential release safe; the reset-work lifetime is\nhandled separately by the following patch.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:00:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:58:56", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81c58a206d1deee01f4c29236d4154c0872f2a38", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/382ee00b2d1e31869ae576a60d3fbe7a2153512f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/739b686aecdb14a6065300ea53401f043e51fd22", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b7d1d8cb1bdca56aecebacd2896615da0acc126a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a045c2f0fbf029873d2295178fa0785ade35af0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/044fca8f45ba9ab6ca526163155234cf88287ff5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ca80328df23f851c86866720d4977783c919ee6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/538c51e9d124cf656f2dd0c0394a8545efc7102d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-68192", "GHSA-52hv-vfrj-x3fv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "65c51ed8-67e8-312f-bdf2-62c358c64233", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "74974521-568c-3b03-83da-d8cfb565f0a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4684997d9eea29380000e062755aa6d368d789a3 <739b686aecdb14a6065300ea53401f043e51fd22"}, {"id": "81d2392b-e657-334e-9c65-729eda2c9298", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4684997d9eea29380000e062755aa6d368d789a3 <5a045c2f0fbf029873d2295178fa0785ade35af0"}, {"id": "8507bc18-0234-37d7-93ef-4e17e68cfb94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "9202d796-b5a5-3930-bf8f-1df3f034a356", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4684997d9eea29380000e062755aa6d368d789a3 <538c51e9d124cf656f2dd0c0394a8545efc7102d"}, {"id": "a52e4d35-7c53-3bf9-9ed9-84c3aa26e416", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}, {"id": "acfe5f8b-e092-3000-8512-12f83cd12987", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "ba2b8796-266d-355d-821c-3dc30b67bfc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "bd338fa8-8978-3b33-9278-9ab6e089103d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "c5a27b61-5d96-33ed-a9af-203f7ea22534", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c5fe9ecb-15f8-3b8e-9811-5f8598918411", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4684997d9eea29380000e062755aa6d368d789a3 <81c58a206d1deee01f4c29236d4154c0872f2a38"}, {"id": "d03be77c-9956-395c-8211-fb23c31d824f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4684997d9eea29380000e062755aa6d3